# API Key Auth — Usage Guide

## 1. Import the module

```typescript
// app.module.ts
import { ApiKeyModule } from './auth/api-key.module';

@Module({
  imports: [
    ApiKeyModule,
    // ... other modules
  ],
})
export class AppModule {}
```

## 2. Add entities to TypeORM

```typescript
// typeorm config
entities: [ApiKeyEntity, ApiKeyAuditLogEntity, /* ...others */]
```

## 3. Apply the guard to webhook routes

```typescript
import { Controller, Post, UseGuards } from '@nestjs/common';
import { ApiKeyGuard } from '../auth/guards/api-key.guard';
import { RequiredScopes } from '../auth/decorators/required-scopes.decorator';
import { ApiKeyScope } from '../auth/entities/api-key.entity';

@Controller('webhooks')
@UseGuards(ApiKeyGuard)
export class WebhooksController {

  @Post('payment-received')
  @RequiredScopes(ApiKeyScope.READ_PAYMENTS)
  handlePayment() { ... }

  @Post('invoice-generate')
  @RequiredScopes(ApiKeyScope.WRITE_INVOICES)
  generateInvoice() { ... }
}
```

## 4. Create an API key (admin only)

```typescript
// Inject ApiKeyService in your admin controller
const { rawKey, entity } = await this.apiKeyService.create({
  name: 'cron-invoicing-service',
  scopes: [ApiKeyScope.WRITE_INVOICES],
  expiresAt: new Date('2027-01-01'),
});

// rawKey is shown ONCE — store it securely in the caller's env
```

## 5. Call a protected endpoint

```bash
curl -X POST https://api.novalabs.com/webhooks/payment-received \
  -H "X-API-Key: <raw_key>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"amount": 100}'
```

## Error responses

| Situation | Status | Message |
|-----------|--------|---------|
| No header | 401 | Missing X-API-Key header |
| Wrong key | 401 | Invalid API key |
| Revoked | 401 | API key has been revoked |
| Expired | 401 | API key has expired |
| Missing scope | 403 | Insufficient scopes. Required: write:invoices |